(6868236, 1034122, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>A rather interesting take that makes one think -the twins seem to be at odds with one another rather than working together. One is lounging on the sofa while the other stands behind and seems to have a catty attitude to her sitting sister. Indeed there is a dilemma here as this pair seems ready to call it quits and split up. Lighting is good on the model(s) but I wish there wasn''t that distracting shadow upon the wall in back...it is almost like a shadowy ''third wheel'' in that it attracts attention away from the main subjects.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. A rather interesting take that makes one think -the twins seem to be at odds with one another rather than working together. One is lounging on the sofa while the other stands behind and seems to have a catty attitude to her sitting sister. Indeed there is a dilemma here as this pair seems ready to call it quits and split up. Lighting is good on the model(s) but I wish there wasn''t that distracting shadow upon the wall in back...it is almost like a shadowy ''third wheel'' in that it attracts attention away from the main subjects.', '2012-09-24 00:20:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6868240, 1034309, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Simple, clean, and stellar in presentation. The overall tan/beige color cast makes me notice and appreciate more the textures and shapes present in the composition. The color hue and the texture also complement the image in that the feel of gritty sand is there which goes rather nicely with the shell and the crab. High marks - very well done.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Simple, clean, and stellar in presentation. The overall tan/beige color cast makes me notice and appreciate more the textures and shapes present in the composition. The color hue and the texture also complement the image in that the feel of gritty sand is there which goes rather nicely with the shell and the crab. High marks - very well done.', '2012-09-24 00:23:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6868249, 1034307, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment now.<br/> <br/>The angle adds to the visual appeal of the composition. Low to the ground, my eye follows the lines and then the feet as I travel ahead to spot the large statue of Taurus/Toro. Processing is nicely done with some nice dynamic tones between darks and lights. The one thing that is a distracting element is that building that rises out from the bulls head - it almost acts like a third horn. Changing angle or getting lower would most likely not get the building out of the shot and it would change the great dynamic arrangement you have here in the shot now. Normally, you would not be able to edit that clock tower out, but with Expert Editing you could if you choose to do so.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment now. The angle adds to the visual appeal of the composition. Low to the ground, my eye follows the lines and then the feet as I travel ahead to spot the large statue of Taurus/Toro. Processing is nicely done with some nice dynamic tones between darks and lights. The one thing that is a distracting element is that building that rises out from the bulls head - it almost acts like a third horn. Changing angle or getting lower would most likely not get the building out of the shot and it would change the great dynamic arrangement you have here in the shot now. Normally, you would not be able to edit that clock tower out, but with Expert Editing you could if you choose to do so.', '2012-09-24 00:32:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6868251, 1034444, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment now.<br/> <br/>Yup, you got me to look up the title and translate it. If google is right then this is a representation of Aquarius. I can see *now* where you are equating this to water but my first impression (and still is) is that it was the crackling of lightning.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment now. Yup, you got me to look up the title and translate it. If google is right then this is a representation of Aquarius. I can see *now* where you are equating this to water but my first impression (and still is) is that it was the crackling of lightning.', '2012-09-24 00:41:08.000000', NULL, 1),
