(6869057, 1034439, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>Very well done composition. Love how you have presented them as they walk down the road (a leading line). The eye follows them as they walk towards the vanishing point. You have some nice warm tones/hues in the shot. I wonder if they really are twins or if the shot was taken at roughly the same time on a different day. They are wearing different jean shorts and the underside of the sneakers is different which make me lean towards the thinking they are twins.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  Very well done composition. Love how you have presented them as they walk down the road (a leading line). The eye follows them as they walk towards the vanishing point. You have some nice warm tones/hues in the shot. I wonder if they really are twins or if the shot was taken at roughly the same time on a different day. They are wearing different jean shorts and the underside of the sneakers is different which make me lean towards the thinking they are twins.', '2012-09-25 10:08:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6869061, 1034308, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Now that is a very bold presentation! I find it interesting how you placed the fish within the sign for Pisces. The bold lines of the pisces sign really draws the eye in and then leads you too the two fish. My first thought was the sign is on it''s side and should be oriented the correct way. However, if you did that, it would change the whole dynamic of the composition because the fish will have to remain placed between those two curves.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Now that is a very bold presentation! I find it interesting how you placed the fish within the sign for Pisces. The bold lines of the pisces sign really draws the eye in and then leads you too the two fish. My first thought was the sign is on it''s side and should be oriented the correct way. However, if you did that, it would change the whole dynamic of the composition because the fish will have to remain placed between those two curves.', '2012-09-25 10:14:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6869063, 1034428, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>The night background is very nicely put together. The human half of the Sagittarius archer is fabulous from the pose to the lighting. The area of the composition that needs a little more work to improve on the composition is the horse half of Sagittarius and way the light falls on the rock shelf he stands upon. First off there is just something that does not appear right about the proportion of the horse half - it torso and back end just seems a little too small or compressed. I could be wrong but to my eye, the back half is like that of a small pony rather than the full sized horse needed to support the weight of the human half. The other thing that would improve on the composition if you used something with actual hair that would have been put in place of the plastic tail. It would just add more realism to the scene. Lastly, the lighting on the underside of the rock shelf is too bright and doesn''t match up with the lighting seen from the other rocks in the distance or the human half of Sagittarius. The position of the light the falls upon those elements is shining down from the top right corner. Still, a good effort and well composed.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  The night background is very nicely put together. The human half of the Sagittarius archer is fabulous from the pose to the lighting. The area of the composition that needs a little more work to improve on the composition is the horse half of Sagittarius and way the light falls on the rock shelf he stands upon. First off there is just something that does not appear right about the proportion of the horse half - it torso and back end just seems a little too small or compressed. I could be wrong but to my eye, the back half is like that of a small pony rather than the full sized horse needed to support the weight of the human half. The other thing that would improve on the composition if you used something with actual hair that would have been put in place of the plastic tail. It would just add more realism to the scene. Lastly, the lighting on the underside of the rock shelf is too bright and doesn''t match up with the lighting seen from the other rocks in the distance or the human half of Sagittarius. The position of the light the falls upon those elements is shining down from the top right corner. Still, a good effort and well composed.', '2012-09-25 10:33:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6869067, 1034437, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>The lighting and focus on the main subject is fabulous. However, there is not enough <u>within</u> the composition to tell me without a shadow of doubt that this is Virgo. I have to take your word for it and the title of what you are telling me. But if you <u>show</u> me that this is Virgo then composition would be stronger for it. It goes by the saying, ''Show, don''t tell''. The wings on the statue make me think that this is more of a representation of an angel rather than the personification of the Zodiac symbol. Taking advantage of the Expert Editing rules one very simple way to accomplish that would to have superimposed/engraved the letter symbol for Virgo on the stone pedestal she stands upon. <br/> <br/>There are, of course, more photo-manip ways to present the statue as Virgo but that would mean removing all the indoor museum background to place her into a setting that would carry the idea that she is Virgo.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. The lighting and focus on the main subject is fabulous. However, there is not enough within the composition to tell me without a shadow of doubt that this is Virgo. I have to take your word for it and the title of what you are telling me. But if you show me that this is Virgo then composition would be stronger for it. It goes by the saying, ''Show, don''t tell''. The wings on the statue make me think that this is more of a representation of an angel rather than the personification of the Zodiac symbol. Taking advantage of the Expert Editing rules one very simple way to accomplish that would to have superimposed/engraved the letter symbol for Virgo on the stone pedestal she stands upon.  There are, of course, more photo-manip ways to present the statue as Virgo but that would mean removing all the indoor museum background to place her into a setting that would carry the idea that she is Virgo.', '2012-09-25 10:53:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6869070, 1034448, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>O.K. am I the only one who sees the two goat heads (for the bottom head, look at the bottom center half which has the head and the blue portions are the ears) in the center of this kaleidoscope composition???? After I get over the center portion that stares me in the face I see all the other textural details of the fish and scales. While it is a different and texturally strong image, I think it suffers from being a little too busy, but that just might be my taste.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. O.K. am I the only one who sees the two goat heads (for the bottom head, look at the bottom center half which has the head and the blue portions are the ears) in the center of this kaleidoscope composition???? After I get over the center portion that stares me in the face I see all the other textural details of the fish and scales. While it is a different and texturally strong image, I think it suffers from being a little too busy, but that just might be my taste.', '2012-09-25 11:00:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6869072, 1033821, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>The whole of this image just speaks ''artsy''. The grain adds a textural feel to this. It also projects the idea that this is a vision from memory or mayhap a moment in time in the distant past. The two children here make me think of the whole Yin/Yang concept as well as the Pisces concept. The two girls are having a conversation and it makes me stop to wonder just what are they talking about. I like how you have the water/sea in the shot for it helps with connecting the visual to the symbol of Pisces. Still, I wish there was just a little more to show a even stronger connection to the zodiac sign. Hmmmm, perhaps if the symbol for Pisces was overlayed in another layer so that it looked like it was drawn in the sand between the two girls.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. The whole of this image just speaks ''artsy''. The grain adds a textural feel to this. It also projects the idea that this is a vision from memory or mayhap a moment in time in the distant past. The two children here make me think of the whole Yin/Yang concept as well as the Pisces concept. The two girls are having a conversation and it makes me stop to wonder just what are they talking about. I like how you have the water/sea in the shot for it helps with connecting the visual to the symbol of Pisces. Still, I wish there was just a little more to show a even stronger connection to the zodiac sign. Hmmmm, perhaps if the symbol for Pisces was overlayed in another layer so that it looked like it was drawn in the sand between the two girls.', '2012-09-25 11:08:26.000000', NULL, 1),
